+/* Above the detection threshold, but too weak to be a finger on a clean
+ * sensor - so it is a finger on a dirty one.
+ *
+ * The background this driver subtracts is read once per activation, and
+ * GOODIX55X4_BACKGROUND_ACCEPT_DIFF above stops an obviously occupied sensor
+ * from replacing a good one. What neither covers is the case where the very
+ * first read of an activation already had a finger on it: that frame becomes
+ * the background, and from then on a real touch differs from it only by the
+ * small amount the finger moved.
+ *
+ * That lands between 100 and 320, which is the trap. It is over the detection
+ * threshold, so the scan reports a touch and captures; and the only escape
+ * from a poisoned background - the poll-exhausted path below, which fires
+ * after ten seconds of seeing nothing - never runs, because something is
+ * always being seen. The session then spends every attempt matching frames
+ * with the fingerprint subtracted out of them.
+ *
+ * Three independent measurements agree on where the gap is:
+ *
+ *   - the threshold comment above, written from bench readings: a real touch
+ *     is around 750
+ *   - patch 0013's own record: every frame taken against a background diff
+ *     below 320 scored 0 against all fifteen enrolled stages, and every match
+ *     came from a diff above 700
+ *   - sixteen real authentications from this machine's journal: the four that
+ *     succeeded read 605, 648, 694, 764 and 790; the twelve that failed read
+ *     106 to 202, and none of them reached ncc 0.48 against a 0.70 threshold
+ *
+ * So a reading in this band is treated as what it is - evidence that the
+ * background is wrong - and the background is discarded so the next scan
+ * calibrates from scratch, exactly as the poll-exhausted path does.
+ *
+ * This only decides which frames are offered to the matcher. It changes no
+ * acceptance criterion and cannot let anything through that would not have
+ * been let through before; a capture rejected here is one that measured
+ * ncc 0.24-0.47 when it was allowed past. */
+#define GOODIX55X4_FINGER_DETECT_CONTAMINATED_MAX 320
+
+/* How long calibration will wait for the finger to come off before giving up.
+ * Only used after a background has been rejected - an ordinary activation
+ * still calibrates on its first read and costs nothing. */
+#define GOODIX55X4_CALIBRATE_MAX_ATTEMPTS 30   /* 3 s at the poll delay below */
+
